<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="Privacy information for the Forfactor corporate website."><PageHero eyebrow="Privacy" title="A simple website with a small data footprint." intro="This corporate website is designed to provide information without requiring accounts, forms or invasive tracking."/>
<section class="section"><div class="shell prose-grid"><p class="eyebrow">Last updated<br/>17 November 2026</p><div class="prose"><h2>Privacy on forfactor.com</h2><h3>Information this site collects</h3><p>This static website does not provide user accounts or a contact form. Forfactor does not intentionally collect personal information through the site itself.</p><p>Like most hosted websites, infrastructure providers may process technical information such as IP addresses, browser details and request logs for security, reliability and delivery.</p><h3>Email</h3><p>If you contact us by email, we will receive the information you choose to include. We use it to respond to your enquiry and manage related correspondence.</p><h3>External websites</h3><p>This site links to product websites and other external services. Their own privacy practices apply when you visit them.</p><h3>Changes</h3><p>We may update this notice when the site or our practices change. The date above identifies the latest revision.</p><h3>Questions</h3><p>For privacy questions, email <a href="mailto:hello@forfactor.com">hello@forfactor.com</a>.</p></div></div></section></BaseLayout>
